<anchor xml:id="_tracy__lz4_8hpp_1aa999858a168415c635eb29be8822ac60"/><section>
    <title>LZ4_FREESTANDING</title>
<indexterm><primary>LZ4_FREESTANDING</primary><secondary>tracy_lz4.hpp</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>tracy_lz4.hpp</primary><secondary>LZ4_FREESTANDING</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput>#define LZ4_FREESTANDING&#160;&#160;&#160;0</computeroutput></para>
<para>LZ4_FREESTANDING : When this macro is set to 1, it enables &quot;freestanding mode&quot; that is suitable for typical freestanding environment which doesn&apos;t support standard C library.</para>

<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>LZ4_FREESTANDING is a compile-time switch.</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>It requires the following macros to be defined: LZ4_memcpy, LZ4_memmove, LZ4_memset.</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>It only enables LZ4/HC functions which don&apos;t use heap. All LZ4F_* functions are not supported.</para>
</listitem><listitem>
<para>See tests/freestanding.c to check its basic setup. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</section>
