<anchor xml:id="_tracy__lz4_8hpp_1a24ddbc39e7379532031a91357e66a32c"/><section>
    <title>LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE</title>
<indexterm><primary>LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE</primary><secondary>tracy_lz4.hpp</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>tracy_lz4.hpp</primary><secondary>LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput>#define LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE&#160;&#160;&#160;<link linkend="_tracy__lz4_8hpp_1a003849b5d7ae53e30ad147fdecc8fab3">LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE_DEFAULT</link></computeroutput></para>
<para>LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE : Memory usage formula : N-&gt;2^N Bytes (examples : 10 -&gt; 1KB; 12 -&gt; 4KB ; 16 -&gt; 64KB; 20 -&gt; 1MB; ) Increasing memory usage improves compression ratio, at the cost of speed. Reduced memory usage may improve speed at the cost of ratio, thanks to better cache locality. Default value is 14, for 16KB, which nicely fits into Intel x86 L1 cache </para>
</section>
